  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_030 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.632 acc / 0.607 F1. Multiprofile with avgpool aggregation is strongly supported (config_002→018, config_018→020), and scvi_n200 shows a modest edge over pca_n2000 (0.632 vs 0.619). However, the fusion method has never been varied—every completed multimodal experiment used concat. Question: Does weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation in the best-performing setting? config_031 changes only the fusion (concat→weighted) relative to config_030, giving a clean single-variable comparison. Why this is the best next experiment: Fusion strategy is a completely untested design axis that could have a larger effect than the ~0.013 encoder difference already observed. Testing it at the current best configuration maximizes information gain: if weighted fusion helps, it identifies a new exploitable direction; if it does not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can redirect budget toward other untested axes (e.g., ViT-L image encoder or scgpt)."
}

